WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.300
Poland's Prime Minister Donald Tusk takes
over from Herman Van Rompuy on the first of

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.780
December as the new President of the European
Council at a pivotal time in the EU's history.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.780
The challenges ahead are formidable. Europe's
economies are only slowly recovering from

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:22.350
the financial crisis. Unemployment is high.
Conflict is simmering in neighbouring Ukraine.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.460
So Tusk has more than a full-time job on his
hands in Brussels, with tasks that are highly

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.430
political and often technical, and he will
also chair summits of leaders in countries

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.420
using the euro currency.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.000
As a first step, the Polish premier must give
up all political posts at home.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.810
He now presides over the European Council,
whose members - the leaders of the EU's 28

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.239
nations have elected him.

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:52.480
The Council sets the EU's political direction
and priorities. But it also handles crisis

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:57.530
management - whether it be economic or in
times of conflict - when decisions must be

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.500
taken at the highest level.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.059
Careful planning is a key to success, as the
president prepares and chairs the summits,

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:10.470
and drives work forward. It's a job that requires
great political skill and an ability to forge

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.260
consensus from 28 points of view.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:22.200
"The interest of each state coincides with
the interests of the European Union.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:26.950
If there wasn't a willingness to reach an agreement, to find a comprise,

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.110
if we didn't have that political will, we wouldn't make it.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.390
So it's my role to facilitate
all that."

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:39.650
Tusk has a mandate for two and a half years.
His term can be renewed once.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:46.650
The Council has four scheduled summits annually
in Brussels but generally meets more often.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:53.290
In the days that follow them, the president
reports to the European Parliament on the

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.180
results.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:02:00.720
His office is in Brussels but the president
also represents the EU on the wider international

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.540
stage, along with the European Commission
president and High Representative.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:10.880
He is the face of the Union, at summits with
major world powers and at the UN General Assembly.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:17.800
"I represent the Union at the highest level.
So what I do is to preside

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:24.200
over meetings that we call our summits with our strategic partners.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.410
These are important meetings."

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:31.879
These tasks, and more, await Donald Tusk - only
the second President of the EU's most powerful

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:36.230
institution - when he takes his bow in Brussels
on the first of December.

